  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Economics of the Chinese Ivory Trade</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In May 2015, the Chinese Government announced that it would strictly control ivory processing and trade until the commercial processing and sale of ivory and its products are eventually halted. A team including economists and other wildlife trade experts will examine how policy changes might affect ivory trade dynamics and poaching pressure. Activities will include two workshops in Beijing and one in Guangzhou to assess variables regarding the scope and timing of such a ban, and drafting recommendations on how the policy could best be implemented to maximize effect in a timely manner.</narrative>
  </description>
